#
# Counter-example for gmeow:ResultObjectConflationConstraint (gmeow:ResultObjectConflation):
# a gmeow:TopologyComputation whose gmeow:producesResult value IS a raw math: object
# (a math:PersistenceDiagram) instead of a gmeow:TopologyResult wrapper that REFERENCES the
# math: object through gmeow:resultArtifact. The consumer-side result is conflated with the
# pure mathematical referent, so the ∀→¬∃ SPARQL constraint (matching the result's type in
# the math: namespace) MUST reject it with shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent. The computation
# asserts no global truth, so the ONLY violation is the conflation.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/semantic-topology/tests/> .

ex:computationBad a gmeow:TopologyComputation ;
    gmeow:producesResult ex:rawDiagram .          # <-- points directly at a raw math: object

ex:rawDiagram a math:PersistenceDiagram .          # the conflated raw math: referent
